{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents</b> — the expression is poetically pleasing at its outset with \"for ascents.\" It is said concerning Israel when they were under siege and distress, or concerning the exiles of our nation." "<b>I lift</b> — it is the way of everyone who is under siege to lift his eyes, perhaps helpers will come to him to drive off the enemy. The word מאין functions like אנה אנחנו עולים (Numbers 14:3, \"where are we going up\"), and there is none like it. הן כולכם מאין — and this form we have not found in a spelling defective of mem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 121, :notes {1 "The citation הן כולכם מאין does not correspond to any standard biblical verse and its relation to the argument about מאין is unclear; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:07.636890971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}